  "notes": {
    "arrival": "Load holds near 400 a minute with short spikes. Within a second it peaks at 47 requests, which is the burst a Poisson generator at the same average almost never makes.",
    "prompts": "Half the prompts are under 6.3K tokens, and one in ten is over 16.8K. The long tail is where prefill time and KV size grow fastest.",
    "turns": "A turn joins a session when its leading block hashes match an earlier request for at least two blocks, using the longest match. 16,644 requests continue an earlier one, and that chain accounts for 97% of all reused blocks.",
    "gaps": "The median follow-up lands under a second later and one in ten waits over 3 minutes. A cache has to hold that context the whole time or the next turn pays full prefill again.",
    "kv": "This trace needs about 22.4 TiB of KV on a dense GQA model and 0.7 TiB on a hybrid model with few attention layers. That gap decides whether host memory is enough or a shared tier is needed."
  },
